ee  Wonder Woman in the DCU in the next  three years and she most likely isn't  going to be played by Gal Gadot and  here's the reason why and here's what to  expect from the first one to three years  of the DCU yes a reboot not entirely of  course I'm assuming characters like  Peacemaker are going to remain but as  far as the Justice League is concerned  yeah pretty much an entire reboot James  Gunn stated that the reason that Henry  Cavill isn't going to be playing  Superman in the DCU is because they're  going to do a Superman Project where  Superman is much younger so that pretty  much tells you a lot about the plan  right there they're going to start the  Justice League from scratch with younger  characters which is a great move we're  going to start off with these characters  they're going to be introduced to us  when they're young we'll see their  Origins I'm sure see what they do in  their youth and of course over the next  eight to ten years they'll grow up their  stories will progress they'll come  together as the Justice League and  pretty much the storytelling and the  Cinematic Universe will be very in sync  and have a lot of continuity which the  old DCU did not have and is pretty much  the main reason that it failed now  speaking of a DCU Justice League reboot  a lot of people have been talking about  Ezra Miller lately this is due to a  report coming from variety they say that  some Warner Brothers executives are open  to the idea of keeping Ezra Miller as  the Flash and yes they are talking about  keeping him after the flash releases on  June 16th of this year 2023. now this  has a lot of people up in commotion  right now because Ezra has gotten into  quite a bit of trouble recently and the  reason that it's very controversial is  because when Johnny Depp got into a  little bit of trouble they fired him  right away and then Johnny even went on  to win the trial against Amber Heard but  he still hasn't been brought back and  Amber Heard wasn't fired 